The bounded Windows non-FMA rotation implementation in
src/chemistry/windows_trigonometry.rs is adapted from AMD's
win-libm sin.asm, cos.asm, and Lsincos_array.asm (MIT license).

Source: https://github.com/amd/win-libm
Commit: 6121d02aef0c775947d5dc655d7fc4ccfe2144ab
Copyright (c) 2002-2019 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.

The Rust adaptation preserves the SSE2 operation ordering for finite attachment
and cleanup rotations in [-2*pi, 2*pi], adds explicit bounds checking and signed-zero
preservation, and omits assembly, FMA dispatch, large-argument reduction,
exception flags, errno handling, and unrelated math functions.
